## Problem
In `server/src/api/sync.rs:150-156, 237-245`, composite primary keys `(id, user_id)` are used for notes. While user_id comes from authenticated ClientInfo, there's no explicit runtime validation before operations.

If ClientInfo extraction were ever bypassed or misconfigured, this could lead to cross-user data access.

## Fix Approach
Add explicit authorization helper and use before sensitive operations:

```rust
// server/src/api/auth_helpers.rs
pub fn verify_note_ownership(
    note_user_id: &str, 
    client_user_id: &str
) -> Result<(), AppError> {
    if note_user_id != client_user_id {
        tracing::warn!(
            note_user = %note_user_id, 
            client_user = %client_user_id, 
            "User ID mismatch in note operation"
        );
        return Err(AppError::Forbidden("Not authorized to access this note".into()));
    }
    Ok(())
}
```

Use before update/delete operations:
```rust
verify_note_ownership(&existing_note.user_id, &client_info.user_id)?;
```

