**Location:** src/lib/services/searchService.ts:24-36

**Problem:** The `indexNotes()` function re-adds all notes to the FlexSearch index but doesn't clear old entries. When a note is deleted, its entry may persist in the index as a 'ghost entry' causing:
- Search returning deleted note IDs
- Stale search results

```typescript
export function indexNotes(notes: DecryptedNote[]): void {
  // Note: FlexSearch Document index doesn't have a clear method
  // So we just re-add all documents (it will update existing ones)

  // BUG: This only updates existing docs, doesn't remove deleted ones!
  notes.forEach((note) => {
    index.add({...});
  });
}
```

**Evidence:** The `removeNote()` function exists (line 53-55) but needs to be called consistently when notes are deleted.

**Remediation:**
1. Ensure `removeNote()` is called in all delete paths (soft delete, permanent delete, sync delete)
2. Or track all indexed IDs and remove any not present in the new notes array:

```typescript
const indexedIds = new Set<string>();

export function indexNotes(notes: DecryptedNote[]): void {
  const newIds = new Set(notes.map(n => n.id));

  // Remove entries no longer present
  for (const id of indexedIds) {
    if (!newIds.has(id)) {
      index.remove(id);
      indexedIds.delete(id);
    }
  }

  // Update/add current notes
  notes.forEach((note) => {
    index.add({ id: note.id, content: note.content, tags: note.tags.join(' ') });
    indexedIds.add(note.id);
  });
}
```

