**Location:** src/lib/services/backupService.ts:1092-1107

**Problem:** The blob URL is revoked synchronously after triggering the download click:

```typescript
const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
// ...
a.href = url;
a.download = filename;
document.body.appendChild(a);
a.click();
document.body.removeChild(a);
URL.revokeObjectURL(url);  // Revoked immediately after click!
```

**Impact:** On slow systems or with large files, the browser may not have finished initiating the download before the URL is revoked, causing download failure.

**Remediation:**
Use a small delay before revoking:

```typescript
a.click();
document.body.removeChild(a);
// Allow time for download to initiate
setTimeout(() => {
  URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
}, 1000);
```

Or use the download attribute completion event if available.

## Problem
In `server/src/error.rs:51-53, 62-64`, DatabaseError and InternalError include full error details that could leak SQL schema information to logs/monitoring.

## Fix Approach
1. Log full errors internally at appropriate log levels
2. Return sanitized generic messages to clients
3. Use structured logging with severity levels

```rust
impl IntoResponse for AppError {
    fn into_response(self) -> Response {
        let (status, client_message) = match &self {
            AppError::DatabaseError(internal_msg) => {
                // Log full details internally
                tracing::error!(error = %internal_msg, "Database error");
                // Return generic message to client
                (StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, "A database error occurred")
            }
            // ...
        };

        (status, Json(json!({ "error": client_message }))).into_response()
    }
}
```

