**Location:** src/lib/services/searchService.ts (entire file)

**Problem:** FlexSearch operations are not wrapped in try-catch. If the search index becomes corrupted or encounters unexpected data:
- The app may crash during search
- No graceful degradation

**Example:**
```typescript
export async function searchNotes(...): Promise<DecryptedNote[]> {
  // No error handling
  const searchResults = await index.searchAsync(searchText, {
    limit: 1000,
    enrich: true,
  });
  // ...
}
```

**Remediation:**
Add error handling with graceful degradation:

```typescript
export async function searchNotes(...): Promise<DecryptedNote[]> {
  try {
    const searchResults = await index.searchAsync(searchText, {...});
    // ... process results
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Search index error:', error);
    // Fallback to basic filtering
    return allNotes.filter(note => 
      note.content.toLowerCase().includes(searchText.toLowerCase())
    );
  }
}
```

